import{_ as e,o as r,c as d,a0 as a}from"./chunks/framework.BTg7EidG.js";const f=JSON.parse('{"title":"Arms & Artifacts","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/artifacts.md","filePath":"guide/artifacts.md"}'),o={name:"guide/artifacts.md"};function s(h,t,i,n,l,c){return r(),d("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[a('<h1 id="arms-artifacts" tabindex="-1">Arms &amp; Artifacts <a class="header-anchor" href="#arms-artifacts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Arms &amp; Artifacts&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Every hero fights with what they carry: <strong>two hand slots and three accessory slots</strong>, filled from what the world gives up. An item&#39;s stats add straight onto the wearer&#39;s own, and speed does double duty: it feeds both battle turns and how far the party marches in a day.</p><h2 id="how-the-slots-work" tabindex="-1">How the slots work <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-the-slots-work" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How the slots work&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Hands</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blade</td><td>1</td><td>Sword, axe, or mace; pairs well with a shield</td></tr><tr><td>Dagger</td><td>1</td><td>Light steel; rogues make pairs of them sing</td></tr><tr><td>Greatblade</td><td>2</td><td>Heavy iron; warriors break the rules with these</td></tr><tr><td>Bow</td><td>2</td><td>Shooters&#39; reach on the tactical field</td></tr><tr><td>Staff</td><td>2</td><td>The caster&#39;s arm</td></tr><tr><td>Shield</td><td>1</td><td>Guard for the off hand (or the main)</td></tr><tr><td>Thrown</td><td>1</td><td><strong>Rogues only.</strong> Corked glassware — see below</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory</td><td>0</td><td>Rings, charms, and lenses; three may be worn</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Two tricks of the trade change everything about who wants what:</p><ul><li><strong>Warriors</strong> are strong enough to wield a two-handed weapon in <em>each</em> hand. Two greatblades on one veteran is the heaviest hitting in the game.</li><li><strong>Rogues</strong> shoot bows <strong>half again as hard</strong> (+50% of the bow&#39;s ranged power), and a <strong>matched pair of daggers</strong> turns them into a whirlwind: +3 melee and +1 speed on top of the steel itself.</li></ul><h3 id="thrown-glassware" tabindex="-1">Thrown glassware <a class="header-anchor" href="#thrown-glassware" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Thrown glassware&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A line nobody else can carry. Corked phials of a thief&#39;s own chemistry: one hand each, so a dagger still fits beside one, and a <strong>reach of 2</strong> — further than a swing, nothing like a bow. You stand just outside a blade&#39;s arc and work from there.</p><p>What makes them worth the hand: <strong>cover counts for nothing against them.</strong> A thicket turns steel, but a phial bursts, and whatever your mark is crouched behind catches it with them. Against an enemy dug into forest or swamp, a rogue with glass is the answer.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Artifact</th><th>Stats</th><th>Where it turns up</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tanglelime Bulb</td><td>🏹+3</td><td>The ring and the wilds</td></tr><tr><td>Weeping Phial</td><td>🏹+4 👟+1</td><td>The blight&#39;s edge</td></tr><tr><td>Bottled Midnight</td><td>🏹+6 👟+1</td><td>The deep blight</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="where-artifacts-come-from" tabindex="-1">Where artifacts come from <a class="header-anchor" href="#where-artifacts-come-from" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Where artifacts come from&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>The fallen.</strong> The victor of any battle strips the dead of their gear. What your enemies carry, you can inherit.</li><li><strong>Hoards.</strong> Marauder-held buildings, and every hold the blight has swallowed, have a 40% chance of yielding an artifact when taken. A hero with <em>Plunder</em> raises that to 60%.</li><li><strong>Dungeon chests.</strong> Storming a garrisoned building on the tactical field ends at the bottom floor with a prize: coin and stores, an artifact, or on rare occasion a caged hero.</li></ul><p><strong>Geography is rarity.</strong> Treasure runs on the same menace scale as garrison muscle: the guild ring and outer wilds yield tier-1 arms, the blight&#39;s edge tier 2, and the deep blight alone gives up the tier-3 relics. Richer finds always mean harder fights.</p><p><strong>Logistics matter.</strong> New finds ride in the finding party&#39;s satchel and can be equipped by that party anywhere. The guild vault opens only inside your own cities: walk the satchel in and <strong>Store all in vault</strong> (or hold one item&#39;s chip to stow just it), or send a rogue to courier it home so another hero can draw from it. Unequipping in the field keeps the piece on the party&#39;s backs.</p><h2 id="the-catalog" tabindex="-1">The catalog <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-catalog" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The catalog&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every Lord sets out armed for their class: the <strong>Guildsteel Blade</strong> (⚔+2), the <strong>Ashwood Bow</strong> (🏹+2), or the <strong>Hermetic Staff</strong> (🏹+2).</p><h3 id="tier-1-·-the-ring-and-the-wilds" tabindex="-1">Tier 1 · the ring and the wilds <a class="header-anchor" href="#tier-1-·-the-ring-and-the-wilds" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tier 1 · the ring and the wilds&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Artifact</th><th>Type</th><th>Stats</th><th>Worth knowing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vitriol Edge</td><td>Blade</td><td>⚔+3</td><td>The best plain sword of the early war</td></tr><tr><td>Aurum Saber</td><td>Blade</td><td>⚔+2 🛡+1</td><td>Steel that pays its own guard</td></tr><tr><td>Cinnabar Cleaver</td><td>Blade</td><td>⚔+4 👟−1</td><td>Heavy chopping at a marching cost</td></tr><tr><td>Quicksilver Dirk</td><td>Dagger</td><td>⚔+2 👟+1</td><td>Half of a rogue&#39;s dream pair</td></tr><tr><td>Salt-Crystal Shiv</td><td>Dagger</td><td>⚔+2</td><td>The other half</td></tr><tr><td>Tin Islands Dirk</td><td>Dagger</td><td>⚔+1 👟+2</td><td>Speed in steel form</td></tr><tr><td>Leaden Maul</td><td>Greatblade</td><td>⚔+5 🛡+1 👟−1</td><td>A wall that swings</td></tr><tr><td>Aether Longbow</td><td>Bow</td><td>🏹+4</td><td>A rogue shoots this at +6</td></tr><tr><td>Reedshaft Bow</td><td>Bow</td><td>🏹+3 👟+1</td><td>Shoot and keep moving</td></tr><tr><td>Philosopher&#39;s Staff</td><td>Staff</td><td>🏹+3 🛡+1</td><td>The working alchemist&#39;s arm</td></tr><tr><td>Calcinator&#39;s Rod</td><td>Staff</td><td>🏹+2 👟+1</td><td>Keeps a frail caster out of reach</td></tr><tr><td>Salt Aegis</td><td>Shield</td><td>🛡+3</td><td>The shield wall made portable</td></tr><tr><td>Verdant Buckler</td><td>Shield</td><td>🛡+2</td><td>Cheap cover for a second line</td></tr><tr><td>Mirror of Mercury</td><td>Shield</td><td>🛡+2 👟+1</td><td>Guard without the slowing</td></tr><tr><td>Amulet of Nigredo</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🛡+2</td><td>Armor with no hands spent</td></tr><tr><td>Winged Philter</td><td>Accessory</td><td>👟+2</td><td>Faster marches for the slowest boot</td></tr><tr><td>Bezoar Charm</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🛡+1 👟+1</td><td>A little of both</td></tr><tr><td>Sharpstone Whetring</td><td>Accessory</td><td>⚔+2</td><td>An edge for any melee hand</td></tr><tr><td>Hawk&#39;s-Eye Lens</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🏹+2</td><td>A shooter&#39;s third eye</td></tr><tr><td>Tincture Bandolier</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🏹+1 👟+1</td><td>For skirmishers on the move</td></tr><tr><td>Firelime Knuckles</td><td>Accessory</td><td>⚔+1 👟+1</td><td>A brawler&#39;s quickness</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="tier-2-·-the-blight-s-edge" tabindex="-1">Tier 2 · the blight&#39;s edge <a class="header-anchor" href="#tier-2-·-the-blight-s-edge" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tier 2 · the blight&#39;s edge&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Artifact</th><th>Type</th><th>Stats</th><th>Worth knowing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Aqua Regia Edge</td><td>Blade</td><td>⚔+4 🛡+1</td><td>The royal solvent, given a hilt</td></tr><tr><td>Nigredo Fang</td><td>Dagger</td><td>⚔+3</td><td>The pair-piece worth marching for</td></tr><tr><td>Greatsword of Sulfur</td><td>Greatblade</td><td>⚔+6</td><td>One in each warrior hand: ⚔+12</td></tr><tr><td>Entropy Reaper</td><td>Greatblade</td><td>⚔+7 🛡−1</td><td>All edge, no apology</td></tr><tr><td>Alkahest Bow</td><td>Bow</td><td>🏹+5 👟+1</td><td>+7 and change in a rogue&#39;s hands</td></tr><tr><td>Stormstring Bow</td><td>Bow</td><td>🏹+6</td><td>A rogue shoots this at +9</td></tr><tr><td>Rod of the Great Work</td><td>Staff</td><td>🏹+4</td><td>Blast fuel for the ambitious</td></tr><tr><td>Staff of the White Work</td><td>Staff</td><td>🏹+3 🛡+2</td><td>The healer-scholar&#39;s defense</td></tr><tr><td>Leaden Bulwark</td><td>Shield</td><td>🛡+4 👟−1</td><td>Bring it to a siege, not a chase</td></tr><tr><td>Ring of the Magnum Opus</td><td>Accessory</td><td>⚔+1 🛡+1</td><td>Quiet, dependable work</td></tr><tr><td>Crucible Girdle</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🛡+3</td><td>Armor for the hands-free</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="tier-3-·-relics-of-the-deep-blight" tabindex="-1">Tier 3 · relics of the deep blight <a class="header-anchor" href="#tier-3-·-relics-of-the-deep-blight" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tier 3 · relics of the deep blight&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Found only near the world&#39;s heart, where the garrisons are cruelest.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Artifact</th><th>Type</th><th>Stats</th><th>Worth knowing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The Decayer&#39;s Edge</td><td>Greatblade</td><td>⚔+10 🛡+1</td><td>The rot&#39;s own harvest blade</td></tr><tr><td>Bow of the Black Work</td><td>Bow</td><td>🏹+8 👟+1</td><td>A rogue shoots this at +12</td></tr><tr><td>Staff of the Seventh Stage</td><td>Staff</td><td>🏹+6 🛡+2</td><td>The Work&#39;s last rung</td></tr><tr><td>Aegis of the Prima Materia</td><td>Shield</td><td>🛡+6</td><td>Nothing gets through first matter</td></tr><tr><td>Philosopher&#39;s Stone Shard</td><td>Accessory</td><td>⚔+2 🏹+2 🛡+2</td><td>Everything, a little</td></tr><tr><td>Twin Fangs of Azoth</td><td>Dagger</td><td>⚔+5 👟+2</td><td>One is a weapon; two are a storm</td></tr><tr><td>Sword of Sol and Luna</td><td>Blade</td><td>⚔+6 🛡+2</td><td>A greatblade&#39;s bite in one hand</td></tr><tr><td>Crown of the Red King</td><td>Accessory</td><td>⚔+3 🛡+3</td><td>Majesty, worn into the melee</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="a-trapper-s-tools" tabindex="-1">A trapper&#39;s tools <a class="header-anchor" href="#a-trapper-s-tools" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A trapper&#39;s tools&quot;">​</a></h3><p>These turn up <strong>only for a party that keeps a Beastmaster</strong> — to anyone else they are so much knotted cord and bone, and the loot table holds them back. Each raises the chance a snared beast is taken alive rather than killed, and they stack: a Beastmaster wearing all three accessory slots is a very hard animal to escape.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Artifact</th><th>Type</th><th>Stats</th><th>Where it turns up</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Knotted Snare-Cord</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🪢+10 capture</td><td>The ring and the wilds</td></tr><tr><td>Whistle of the Vats</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🪢+15 capture 👟+1</td><td>The ring and the wilds</td></tr><tr><td>Beast-Whisper Torc</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🪢+22 capture 🛡+1</td><td>The blight&#39;s edge</td></tr><tr><td>Muzzle of Quiet Hours</td><td>Accessory</td><td>🪢+30 capture 🛡+2</td><td>The deep blight</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="consumables" tabindex="-1">Consumables <a class="header-anchor" href="#consumables" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consumables&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Draughts and charters are <strong>spent in the using</strong>, never worn. They ride in the satchel and <strong>stack</strong>: three of the same bottle are one line and a count, not three slots. Pour them from the <strong>Skills</strong> sheet, which offers each to whoever in the column most needs it.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Consumable</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Draught of Red Lead</td><td>Restores 40% of the drinker&#39;s health</td></tr><tr><td>Greater Draught of Red Lead</td><td>80% of it</td></tr><tr><td>Draught of Quicksilver</td><td>Restores 50% of the drinker&#39;s Essence</td></tr><tr><td>Greater Draught of Quicksilver</td><td>Refills the pool entirely</td></tr><tr><td>Charter of the Furrow</td><td>Sows one field. Any hero can present it — a farm hand&#39;s charge in a satchel</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Since arts now cost Essence and Essence only comes back on your own ground, quicksilver is what keeps a hero working while the campaign is far from home. A rogue with <strong>Steal</strong> can lift one straight off a foe.</p><h3 id="the-philosopher-s-stone" tabindex="-1">The Philosopher&#39;s Stone <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-philosopher-s-stone" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Philosopher&#39;s Stone&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Artifact</th><th>Type</th><th>Stats</th><th>Worth knowing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The Philosopher&#39;s Stone</td><td>Accessory</td><td>⚔+3 🏹+3 🛡+3 · <strong>Essence never runs out</strong></td><td>The Great Work itself, in the hand</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The one artifact the whole Work is named for. Its bearer&#39;s <strong>Essence is bottomless</strong> — but the working is not free: it comes out of <em>them</em> instead, a third of what it would have cost in Essence, paid in blood. The toll alone can never be the blow that kills them, so an alchemist holding the Stone can cast all day; they simply bleed for it.</p><p>It is on no loot table. Only the <strong>deepest vault</strong> can hold it — the bottom floor of a tier-3 hold in the deep blight — and even there it comes up about <strong>one time in twenty-five</strong>. Whole campaigns finish without one. If you find it, it goes on your Lord.</p><h2 id="kitting-a-hero" tabindex="-1">Kitting a hero <a class="header-anchor" href="#kitting-a-hero" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Kitting a hero&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>A <strong>warrior Lord</strong> wants two greatblades and armor accessories: the Entropy Reaper pair (⚔+14) with a Crucible Girdle covers the lost guard.</li><li>A <strong>rogue</strong> wants the best bow in the world plus paired daggers held in reserve, with speed accessories to strike first and slip away.</li><li>An <strong>alchemist</strong> stays alive by reach: a defensive staff, then the Winged Philter or Mirror-adjacent guard so the melee never arrives.</li><li>Remember the party marches at its <strong>slowest member&#39;s</strong> speed: one 👟−1 item on the wrong unit slows the whole column.</li></ul>',36)])])}const u=e(o,[["render",s]]);export{f as __pageData,u as default};
